[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Rapport-Jobava System, ...a6"]
[ECO "D01"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "fork"]
[Themes "c7-square,queenside-space"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2.Nc3 and 3.Bf4"]
[Start "orthodox 1...d5"]

2. Nc3 Nf6 { Develops and attacks nothing yet, but it prepares ...Bf5 or ...e6 and keeps d5 covered. } 3. Bf4 a6 { Takes the b5 square away from the knight. From b5 it would jump to c7 and fork the king and rook. } 4. e3 ( 4. Nf3 e6 5. e3 c5 ) 4... e6 { Supports d5 and opens a diagonal for the bishop on f8. } 5. Nf3 c5 { Hits d4, which the bishop on f4 cannot guard. Meanwhile the pawn on a6 still keeps the knight off b5. } 6. Be2 Nc6 { Adds a second attacker to d4. } 7. O-O Be7 { Gets the king ready to castle. After ...O-O, trade on d4 if White allows it and play ...b5 to gain space; the knight on c3 cannot go to b5. } *
